ots":{"content":[{"config":{"icon":"layout-dashboard","label":{"$i18n":"nav.overview"},"selected":false},"id":"tab-overview","type":"TabBarItem"},{"config":{"icon":"app-window","label":{"$i18n":"nav.views"},"selected":false},"id":"tab-views","type":"TabBarItem"},{"config":{"icon":"workflow","label":{"$i18n":"nav.flows"},"selected":false},"id":"tab-flows","type":"TabBarItem"},{"config":{"badge":"5","badgeTone":"annotation","icon":"inbox","label":{"$i18n":"nav.reviews"},"selected":true},"id":"tab-reviews","type":"TabBarItem"}]},"type":"TabBar"}]},"type":"Stack"}]},"type":"RootShell"},"name":"Reviews inbox","spec":{"accessibility":["The queue is a list of buttons; the selected row exposes aria-current and an Iris inset bar in addition to its tint.","The detail pane is a labelled region and the phone thread sheet a labelled dialog with a visible close button; focus moves into the sheet on open and back to the row on close.","Thread status uses an icon and a word, never color alone; counts are announced with their label.","Phone tier rows, inputs and actions use 44px targets and 16px input text so iOS does not zoom.","No text renders below 12px in any Locale; controls use 13px and prose 14px, and zh-TW line heights grow by about 2px.","Light and dark themes meet WCAG 2.2 AA contrast for text and controls."],"constraints":["The Reviews inbox is a page, never a duplicate side panel next to the canvas Comments panel (The Same Place Rule).","Actors and timestamps on Review records are stamped by the server from the authenticated member; the UI never sends them.","Visual language follows the Quiet Canvas design system in DESIGN.md: graphite chrome, Iris violet only for selection, focus and the single primary action per region, Marker magenta only for human annotation, and status hues only in badges, icons and alerts.","Every visible string is bound with $i18n. en-US and zh-TW keep identical key sets; zh-TW uses Taiwan Traditional Chinese with full-width punctuation and keeps domain nouns (View, Variant, Widget, Workspace, Review, Spec, UX Flow, Handoff, Adapter, Locale, Asset, Decision, Owner, Checks, Evidence) in English.","Identities and measurements stay literal and use the mono blueprint register: Widget ids such as #checkout-submit, Widget type names, revisions, keyboard keys and CLI commands are never translated."],"decisions":[],"entryConditions":["A signed-in member chose Reviews in the Rail or TabBar, followed \"waiting for review\" from the Overview, or opened a thread deep link.","Review threads are read through the shared application facade; the queue never keeps browser-owned canonical state.","The render context selects one Workspace viewport preset (desktop 1920 × 1080, tablet 1024 × 768, or mobile 390 × 844), one Locale (en-US default or zh-TW), and one theme (light or dark). All twelve combinations are authored and captured explicitly."],"intent":"Give reviewers one queue of every Review thread that needs a human verdict: scan, read, reply and resolve from a master–detail layout on desktop, and from a home list plus a thread sheet on phones.","interactionRules":["The queue groups threads into Ready for review, then Open, newest activity first; each row shows a status icon, the starter (initials or a bot glyph for agents), a one-line title, relative time, an annotation-colored message count, the View name and the mono anchor and change-domain chips.","Tabs filter the queue to Inbox, Ready, Open or Resolved with counts; Search filters by text and \"/\" focuses it; Mine and Updated are quick filters.","The header count (\"5 waiting\") counts every unresolved thread in the Inbox tab, ready for review plus open; the Overview headline reports the same queue split into \"waiting for review\" and \"open\", so the two always add up.","On desktop and tablet, selecting a row shows the thread in the detail pane (master–detail): header with status and target chip, \"Open in canvas\", the timeline, a reply field with ⌘↵, \"Submit for review…\" and a solid Resolve with its resolution hint.","On phones the queue is the home screen; selecting a row opens the thread in a bottom sheet with the reply field, a full-width Resolve and a close control (thread-sheet Variant).","J and K move through the queue, R focuses reply, E resolves and O opens the thread on the canvas; the key legend sits at the foot of the queue on desktop.","Resolve is human-only. Agents may reply and submit ready for review, but the Resolve control is shown only to signed-in members whose role allows it.","When nothing is waiting, the queue shows \"Nothing waiting for review\" with one next action, and the detail pane shows \"Select a thread\" (empty-inbox Variant).","Layout derives from the viewport width only: 1280px and wider shows the 264px Rail, the main region and (where present) a 340px right panel; 640–1279px collapses the Rail to a 56px icon rail and moves the right panel to on-demand; below 640px the Rail is replaced by the 56px bottom TabBar."],"references":[{"label":"Direct resolve of discussion threads (human-only, Workbench-only)","relation":"decision","type":"external","uri":"https://github.com/DevilTea/uiux/discussions/7#discussioncomment-18757815"},{"label":"Review pin display hint","relation":"decision","type":"external","uri":"https://github.com/DevilTea/uiux/discussions/7#discussioncomment-18757814"},{"label":"Member identity, roles, tokens and agent edit leases","relation":"decision","type":"external","uri":"https://github.com/DevilTea/uiux/discussions/1#discussioncomment-18758344"},{"label":"LAN/team access, authentication and reviewer identity","relation":"decision","type":"external","uri":"https://github.com/DevilTea/uiux/discussions/1#discussioncomment-18757820"},{"relation":"open-in-canvas","type":"view","variantName":"thread-open","viewId":"7f3d7780-3cb9-4e57-8f0b-2e8d569905c1"}]},"variants":{"empty-inbox":{"state":{"detail-empty":{"visible":true},"detail-thread":{"open":false},"queue-empty-wrap":{"visible":true},"queue-list":{"visible":false}}},"thread-sheet":{"state":{"r2":{"selected":true},"thread-sheet":{"open":true}}}}}
